  <text>
      <body>
         <entry xml:id="istrofomta-dlgenr"
            xml:lang="en"
            type="mainEntry"
            prev="#"
            next="#"
            source="Genesis Rabbah">
            <form type="lemma" opt="false">
               <orth type="lemma" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false" select="true">אסטרופומטא</orth>
               <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">ʾsṭrwpwmṭʾ</orth>
               <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">isṭrofomṭaʾ</pron>
               <gramGrp opt="false">
                  <gram type="pos" opt="false">noun</gram>
                  <gram type="gen" opt="false">f.</gram>
               </gramGrp>
               <form type="variant" opt="false">
                  <orth type="variant" xml:lang="jpa" opt="false">אסטרופומטה</orth>
                  <orth type="transliteration" xml:lang="fjb" opt="false">ʾsṭrwpwmth</orth>
                  <pron notation="rabbinic" opt="false">isṭrofomtah</pron>
               </form>
            </form>
            <sense xml:id="istrofomta-dlgenr-1">
               <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en" subtype="sense">
                  <quote>hinge, a door which can be opened to both sides</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="translationEquivalent" xml:lang="grc">
                  <quote>στροφώματος</quote>
               </cit>
               <cit type="example" xml:lang="jpa">
                  <quote>אמר ר' אייבו פלונו שלאבינו יצחק מפולש היה, רבנין אמ' כמין 
                  <app>
                     <lem>אסטרופומטה</lem>
                     <rdg wit="#Vat1">אסתרופומטה</rdg>
                     <rdg wit="#Ox1">איסטרופימטא</rdg>
                     <rdg wit="#Ox2">איסתריפימטא</rdg>
                     <rdg wit="#V">איסטרופומיטא</rdg>
                     <rdg wit="#K">איצטריבומטא</rdg>
                     <rdg wit="#Vat2"> איסתרופומטה</rdg>
                  </app> הדלתות היו נכפלות לאחוריהן, עמד לו יעקב אחרי הדלת עד שנכנס עשו ויצא לן</quote>
                  <bibl>
                     <ref type="witness">66,5</ref>
                     <ref type="witness">II 750: 1</ref>
                  </bibl>
                  <ref type="entry" xml:lang="jpa">פלונו</ref>
                  <cit type="translation" xml:lang="en">
                     <quote>R. Aibo said: The tent of our father Isaac was open to both sides. The Rabbis said: it was like an “isṭrofomṭaʾ” – the doors could be opened backwards. Jacob stood behind the door until Esau came in and then he departed.</quote>
                  </cit>
                  <note>= <bibl type="ancient">Yalq 115 (ΙΙ 557: 67)</bibl></note>
               </cit>
            </sense>
            <note>In <bibl type="ancient">mMid 4,1</bibl> as <term xml:lang="jpa">איצטרמיטה</term>. <bibl type="modern">Levy I 123b</bibl>; <bibl type="modern">Krauss, LW II 82b</bibl>: Gr. <term xml:lang="grc">στροφώματος</term>; <bibl type="modern">Fleischer I 282</bibl> and <bibl type="modern">Jastrow I 91b</bibl> see the source in Gr. pl. <term xml:lang="grc">στροφώματα</term>. Heijmanns regards <term xml:lang="jpa">א(צ)טרפמיטה</term> <term xml:lang="fjb">ʾ(ṣ)ṭrfmyṭn</term> <term xml:lang="rabbinic">ʾi(ṣ)ṭrafamitah</term> as the original reading.</note>
            <ref type="bibliography">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Heijmanns (2013)</title>
                  <citedRange>31-31</citedRange>
               </bibl>
            </ref>
         </entry>
      </body>
